Source: homelab-developer
Section: web
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), perl (>= 5.36), libmojolicious-perl, libyaml-libyaml-perl
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-developer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nginx
Description: developer.mailmasker.org, the MailMasker API reference
 Every ability of the MailMasker API (homelab-api and the services behind
 it): what it does, who may use it, its parameters, an example answer, and
 ready-to-run examples in cURL, Perl and homelab-cli. Each page is also
 Markdown, indexed by llms.txt, and a Claude Code skill (skill/SKILL.md)
 looks calls up there as it works.
 .
 The site is built when the package is, from reference/*.yml, and checked
 against the code it documents: every route reachable through the api must
 have an entry saying who may really use it, or the build fails. The host
 serving it runs only nginx.
 .
 An API call homelab-cli makes is documented here first; homelab-cli's own
 build fails on a call this reference does not have.
